{
  "description": "Shared test vectors of the nym_auth mdoc challenge (SPEC.md section 3): the SessionTranscript (the transcript seed) and e2, the SHA-256 of the device-authentication message. Byte-identical in zk-cred-vega and zk-cred-longfellow. min_nonce_chars is the shortest nonce derive accepts. derive_redirect and rejects_redirect (added for the OpenID4VPHandover of a presentation delivered by redirect or QR, response_uri, OpenID4VP 1.0 appendix B.2.6.1) are additive: derive and rejects keep their meaning, and a consumer that does not implement the redirect handover ignores both new arrays. Over redirects the response MUST be encrypted, so the JWK thumbprint is always 32 bytes and a null one is in rejects_redirect (the DC API handover keeps null for an unencrypted response). Each derive_redirect entry gives the CBOR of OpenID4VPHandoverInfo, the SessionTranscript and e2; the digest of the transcript alone is e2 for either handover.",
